Since we have the root README.md locked in, let’s tackle the initial physical definition for Track B (Modular Micro-Stack). To establish this layout, we need to account for space and signal pin assignments across a 3-layer sandwich stack.
Here is a comprehensive breakdown of the layer mappings, pin allocations, and physical clearance parameters to push straight into your new repo.

1. Physical Dimensions & Mechanical Budget

Micro-whoops live and die by mechanical packaging constraints. For a sub-20g build, you must define the following clearance profiles:
• Mounting Pattern: Standardized 16mm x 16mm with M2 through-holes.
• Stack Vertical Height: Maximum 11mm total height (including rubber anti-vibration grommets) to fit comfortably beneath a micro injection-molded or 3D-printed canopy.
• Inter-layer Spacing: 3.5mm nylon or TPU spacers between boards to ensure adequate airflow and prevent surface components from rubbing against adjacent PCB layers.

2. The Three-Layer Pinout Architecture

Because we are discarding bulky plastic pin headers to save weight, all interconnects between these layers will be jumped using short, direct-solder lengths of ultra-flexible 30AWG silicone wire.
