3. Comprehensive Pin Assignment Breakdown


Layer 1 (Bottom): OpenESC Micro (4-in-1 Speed Controller)

This board interfaces directly with the high-current 1S battery source and distributes clean, regulated voltage to the rest of the stack.
• Primary Power Pads: Heavy-duty, exposed tinned copper pads for soldering the main BT2.0 / NX69 battery pigtail (1S LiPo input: 3.0V – 4.4V).
• Power Distribution Bus: Outbound micro solder pads providing continuous 5V @ 1.5A Regulated DC to power the upper flight controller layer.
• Signal Input Pads: A linear 4-pad row mapping motor control inputs directly from the FC outputs: M1_PWM, M2_PWM, M3_PWM, M4_PWM.
• Motor Output Pads: Three separate, wide-trace solder pads on each corner of the board (Phase_A, Phase_B, Phase_C) for direct connection to the brushless motor windings, completely eliminating heavy plastic JST plugs.

Layer 2 (Middle): OpenFC Micro (Flight Computer)

The central intelligence unit processing tracking telemetry and stabilization loops.
• Power Input Bus: Inbound 5V and GND pads tied straight to the Layer 1 regulator output.
• Actuator Control Pads: Outbound M1, M2, M3, and M4 control pads positioned natively on the perimeter to minimize wiring distances down to Layer 1.
• Receiver Telemetry Port (UART 1): Dedicated serial link routing to the OpenRX module: 5V, GND, TX1 (Telemetry), and RX1 (Control Data).
• Video Peripheral Port (UART 2): Dedicated serial port for camera OSD configurations and video control: 5V, GND, TX2 (SmartAudio protocol for changing VTX power/channels via radio), and CAM_IN (analog video signal feed).
• Video Processing Core: An onboard MAX7456 OSD chip routing a clean, telemetry-overlaid video signal out via a dedicated VTX_OUT pad.

Layer 3 (Top): OpenRX-ELRS & Analog VTX Module

Combining the radio frequency elements on the top layer isolates sensitive wireless links from the switching magnetic noise of the bottom layer's ESC FETs.
• ExpressLRS Receiver Node: Uses basic 5V, GND, TX, and RX pads running CRSF protocol data down into the Layer 2 UART 1 hub.
• Analog Video Transmitter Node: Powered by either raw battery voltage or 5V (depending on whether you select a high-output 400mW VTX core). It includes GND, SmartAudio (wired to Layer 2's TX2), and VIDEO_IN (wired to Layer 2's VTX_OUT).
